 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "The session cookie uses a tagging layer on top of JSON, in `src/tessel/json/tag.py`.\n\n**Classes**\n- **`TypedCookieSerializer`** (`tag.py:219`) is the serializer.\n  - `dumps` (L321) tags the value and writes compact JSON.\n  - `loads` (L325) parses the JSON, then `_untag_scan` (L309) walks it recursively and converts tagged dicts back to Python objects.\n  - Tag classes are tried in order, and `register()` (L256) adds new ones.\n- **`TypeMarker`** (`tag.py:60`) is the base class for tags. Each tag has a `key`, `check`, `to_json` and `to_python`. `tag()` wraps the converted value as `{key: json_value}`.\n- **Built-in tags**, from `default_tags` (L238):\n  - **`TagTuple`** (key `\" t\"`): becomes a list in JSON and `tuple(...)` on load.\n  - **`TagBytes`** (`\" b\"`): base64 string, decoded back to `bytes`.\n  - **`TagDateTime`** (`\" d\"`): HTTP date string, parsed back with `parse_date`.\n  - Also `TagUUID`, `TagMarkup`, `TagDict` (escapes dicts that look like tags) and the `PassDict`/`PassList` pass-throughs.\n\nThe keys start with a space (`\" t\"`, `\" b\"`, `\" d\"`) so they don't collide with ordinary one-key dicts. `untag` only converts single-key dicts whose key is a registered tag.\n\n**Wiring into the session**\n- `src/tessel/sessions.py:273` creates `session_json_serializer = TypedCookieSerializer()`.\n- `SignedCookieSessionInterface` (L284) sets `serializer = session_json_serializer` (L300) and passes it into the `itsdangerous` signing serializer (L316). The cookie is therefore tagged JSON that is also signed.",
